From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?John=20T=C3=B6rnblom?= <john.tornblom@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:01:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ps4: a video driver on Mesa: OpenGL, OpenGL ES and Vulkan

The display is drawn on by the GPU only, through Mesa, which owns VideoOut:
OpenGL and OpenGL ES 2 through EGL (zink on RADV, EGL's videoout
platform), and Vulkan (RADV) through VK_KHR_display. There is no software
framebuffer: windows drawn in software (SDL_GetWindowSurface(), the
software renderer) are presented by SDL through its OpenGL or OpenGL ES
renderer.

The display has Mesa's one mode, 1920x1080 at 60 Hz, and a window is
always the whole screen, whatever size it is created or set to (as with
KMSDRM): it is resized to the display and the program gets
SDL_WINDOWEVENT_RESIZED.

- OpenGL and OpenGL ES: libEGL.so.1, with libGLESv2.so.2 for OpenGL ES, are
  dlopen()ed when a program first asks for a GL window; the display is
  EGL_DEFAULT_DISPLAY, and any non-zero native window is the screen. Mesa
  has no libGL on the PS4, so OpenGL functions come from
  eglGetProcAddress(). The OpenGL and OpenGL ES 2 renderers are built.
- Vulkan: libvulkan.so.1 (RADV, there is no loader) is dlopen()ed; a
  window's surface is a display plane surface (VK_KHR_surface and
  VK_KHR_display).
- Mesa's libraries stay loaded once loaded: they register atexit()
  handlers, and keep VideoOut and its framebuffers for the whole process.
- A USB or Bluetooth keyboard (libSceKeyboard) gives key events, and text
  input on a US layout. The on-screen keyboard is the IME dialog
  (libSceImeDialog), whose UTF-16 text is sent as text input, followed by
  Return. Both libraries are loaded with libSceSysmodule.
- A media remote on libScePad's remote control port gives the arrow keys,
  Return, Escape and Menu, from what it reports as the controller's
  buttons. The PS4 has no HDMI-CEC remote, so there is no CEC key table.
- The splash screen is hidden when video starts.

docs/README-ps4.md describes the port.

