diff --git a/docs/README-ps4.md b/docs/README-ps4.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..6d71b8059
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/README-ps4.md
@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+PS4
+===
+SDL port for the Sony PlayStation 4, built with the
+[ps4-homebrew-dev SDK](https://github.com/ps4-homebrew-dev/sdk).
+
+Graphics are drawn by the GPU only, through Mesa: OpenGL and OpenGL ES 2
+through EGL (zink), and Vulkan (RADV) through `VK_KHR_display`. There is no
+software framebuffer of SDL's own: windows drawn in software
+(`SDL_GetWindowSurface()`, the software renderer) are presented by SDL
+through its OpenGL or OpenGL ES renderer.
+
+Building
+--------
+With the SDK installed (`PS4_HOMEBREW_SDK`, by default `/opt/ps4-homebrew-sdk`):
+```
+   source "${PS4_HOMEBREW_SDK}/toolchain/orbis.sh"
+   ${CMAKE} -S. -Bbuild -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
+   ${MAKE} -C build
+   ${MAKE} -C build install DESTDIR="${SYSROOT}"
+```
+SDL is a static library; link it with `orbis-pkg-config --libs sdl2`, which
+adds the system libraries it calls (libScePad, libSceUserService,
+libSceSystemService and libSceSysmodule).
+
+Drivers
+-------
+* Video (`ps4`): one display, 1920x1080 at 60 Hz, Mesa's one VideoOut mode.
+  A window always fills it, whatever size it is created or set to, and the
+  program gets `SDL_WINDOWEVENT_RESIZED`.
+  * OpenGL and OpenGL ES: `libEGL.so.1` and `libGLESv2.so.2` are loaded when
+    a program first asks for a GL window. Mesa has no `libGL` there; OpenGL
+    functions come from `eglGetProcAddress()`.
+  * Vulkan: `libvulkan.so.1` (RADV) is loaded; `SDL_Vulkan_GetInstanceExtensions()`
+    asks for `VK_KHR_surface` and `VK_KHR_display`, and the window's surface
+    is a display plane surface.
+  * Mesa's libraries stay loaded once loaded: they keep VideoOut, and
+    register `atexit()` handlers, for the whole process.
+  * They are found where the SDK's `dlopen()` looks: the system's library
+    folders, `/app0/sce_module/`, then the current folder.
+* Audio (`ps4`): libSceAudioOut's main port, 48 kHz, 16-bit or float, mono,
+  stereo or 7.1.
+* Joystick (`ps4`): the DualShock 4 of each user logged in, one joystick per
+  login slot (its player index), named after the user, with a game
+  controller mapping of its own (a PS4 controller to SDL). The touch pad, the
+  accelerometer, the gyroscope, rumble and the light bar are supported. The
+  PS and SHARE buttons belong to the system, so there is no guide and no back
+  button.
+* Keyboard: a USB or Bluetooth keyboard (libSceKeyboard), as key events, and
+  as text input on a US layout. The on-screen keyboard is the system's IME
+  dialog: `SDL_StartTextInput()` opens it, and the text typed in it is sent
+  as text input, followed by a press of Return.
+* Remote: what a media remote reports on libScePad's remote control port as
+  the controller's arrows, X, O and OPTIONS, as the arrow keys, Return,
+  Escape and Menu.
+* Filesystem: `SDL_GetBasePath()` is the program's folder (from `argv[0]`,
+  or `/app0/` in a package); `SDL_GetPrefPath()` is in `$XDG_DATA_HOME`,
+  which the SDK's crt sets before `main()`.
+* Locale: the system language. `SDL_OpenURL()` opens the web browser.
+
+libSceAudioOut, libSceKeyboard and libSceImeDialog have no link stubs in the
+SDK: SDL loads them with libSceSysmodule when it first needs them.
